---
---

<div id="panel-connect" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-8">
  <div class="text-center space-y-6">
    <!-- Badge -->
    <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-wxm-storm/40 border border-wxm-cloud/20 text-wxm-cloud text-xs font-medium">
      <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 animate-pulse"></span>
      <span class="font-semibold text-white">Official WG1200 Gateway Switcher</span>
    </div>

    <!-- Title & Tagline -->
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">
        Keep it a <span class="text-white">WeatherXM tri-protocol gateway</span><br class="hidden sm:inline" />
        or turn it into a <span class="text-emerald-400">full Meshtastic node</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-wxm-mist max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        In WeatherXM mode, your paired weather station can publish to WeatherXM, Meshtastic and MeshCore at the same time. In Full Meshtastic mode, the WG1200 itself becomes a native Meshtastic router/repeater. Switch safely over USB; WeatherXM identity, cloud credentials and the factory recovery slot remain intact.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Product Image (WG1200 Gateway with clean transparent background) -->
    <div class="relative py-2 flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
      <div class="relative flex items-center justify-center">
        <!-- Subtle backplate aura -->
        <div class="absolute w-48 h-48 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 blur-2xl pointer-events-none"></div>
        <img
          src="/wg1200-gateway.png"
          alt="WeatherXM WG1200 Gateway"
          class="relative w-40 sm:w-44 h-auto drop-shadow-[0_12px_24px_rgba(0,0,0,0.6)] pointer-events-none select-none"
        />
      </div>

      <!-- Device Specification Info (Unmistakable Green Ready State) -->
      <div class="mt-3 flex items-center space-x-2 text-xs select-none">
        <span class="indicator-dot-green animate-pulse"></span>
        <span class="text-wxm-cloud font-semibold">Compatible Hardware:</span>
        <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono font-medium">WeatherXM D1 / WG1200 (ESP32-S3 16MB)</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Primary Action Center (Unmistakable Green Action Box) -->
    <div class="max-w-md mx-auto p-6 rounded-card bg-wxm-midnight/90 border-2 border-emerald-500/40 backdrop-blur-md shadow-card text-center space-y-4">
      <div class="space-y-1">
        <span class="text-[11px] font-extrabold text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Step 1 — USB Connection</span>
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white">Connect Gateway over USB</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-wxm-mist">
          Connect your WG1200 via USB-C to your computer, then click the green button below to authorize the serial port.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Dual USB Device Explanation Notice -->
      <div class="text-left p-3.5 rounded-lg bg-wxm-abyss/80 border border-wxm-cloud/15 space-y-2 text-xs">
        <div class="flex items-center space-x-2 text-emerald-400 font-semibold text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
          <span>Two USB Devices Will Appear</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-wxm-mist leading-relaxed text-[11px]">
          The WG1200 exposes two USB serial interfaces in the browser port selector:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-[11px] text-wxm-cloud pl-1">
          <li class="flex items-start space-x-1.5">
            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold">1.</span>
            <span><strong class="text-white">USB-Serial (CH340)</strong> <span class="text-emerald-400 font-semibold">(Recommended)</span> — Hardware UART bridge for flashing & console logs.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start space-x-1.5">
            <span class="text-wxm-mist font-bold">2.</span>
            <span><strong class="text-white">USB JTAG / Serial (ESP32-S3)</strong> — Native on-chip USB peripheral.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-[10px] text-wxm-mist/90 italic pt-0.5">
          Tip: Select <strong>USB-Serial (CH340)</strong>. If it fails to respond or is busy, try the other port.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col items-center space-y-3 pt-1">
        <!-- THE UNMISTAKABLE VIBRANT GREEN CONNECT BUTTON -->
        <button
          id="btn-connect"
          type="button"
          class="w-full py-4 px-6 rounded-control font-black text-base btn-primary-green flex items-center justify-center space-x-3 cursor-pointer active:scale-[0.99] focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-emerald-400 focus:ring-offset-2 focus:ring-offset-wxm-midnight select-none shadow-lg"
        >
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-wxm-abyss" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" />
          </svg>
          <span class="tracking-wide">Connect WG1200 Gateway</span>
        </button>

        <button
          id="btn-connect-manual"
          type="button"
          class="text-xs text-wxm-mist hover:text-white underline underline-offset-4 decoration-wxm-cloud/30 hover:decoration-white transition-colors cursor-pointer"
        >
          Device not appearing? Select serial port manually →
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Connection Error Callout -->
    <div id="connect-error-banner" class="hidden text-left p-4 rounded-card border border-wxm-error/40 bg-wxm-error/10 text-white space-y-2.5 mt-4 max-w-xl mx-auto">
      <div class="flex items-start space-x-2.5">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-wxm-error flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/>
        </svg>
        <div class="flex-1">
          <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-white" id="connect-error-title">Connection Failed</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-wxm-cloud/90 mt-1" id="connect-error-detail"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-[11px] text-wxm-mist bg-wxm-abyss/80 p-3 rounded-control border border-wxm-cloud/10 space-y-1.5">
        <p class="font-semibold text-wxm-cloud">Troubleshooting tips:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Two USB devices appear:</strong> Select <strong>USB-Serial (CH340)</strong>. If it fails or is busy, try <strong>USB JTAG / Serial</strong>.</li>
          <li>Ensure no other application (PlatformIO, Arduino IDE, serial monitor) is holding the serial port open.</li>
          <li><strong>Manual Bootloader Mode:</strong> Hold down the <span class="text-white font-semibold">BOOT</span> button on the WG1200 while connecting the USB cable (or while pressing RESET), then release BOOT and click Connect.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
